II. West of the International Date Line is always a day later than east of the line.
III. The Earth turns 15° of longitude in an hour.
Which of the statements given above is/are correct?$q$,$q$I and II only$q$,$q$I and III only$q$,$q$II and III only$q$,$q$III only$q$,$q$1a75b3513d3e2b3237c601a0ec085774915d55a6ce40db69f40bdea42e3fadab$q$,$q$C$q$,'MODEL_ONLY',$q$dp-solved://NDA_2026_II_GAT_GK_SET_A$q$,null,$q$C$q$,$q$C$q$,false,$q$Geography$q$,$q$Physical Geography$q$,$q$Earth Motions & Geographical Coordinates$q$,$q$Date line and rotation$q$,'Knowledge',$q$3-Statement Combination$q$,$q$PATTERN.STATEMENT.3$q$,$q$I is false: the Prime Meridian is $0^\circ$ and the Date Line is near $180^\circ$.
